## Node.js Web App for Multi-Level Marketing Scheme

```js
const express = require('express');
const mongoose = require('mongoose');

const app = express();
app.use(express.json());

const products = [
  {
    name: 'Gold Package',
    price: 199,
    level: 3,
  },
  {
    name: 'Silver Package',
    price: 99,
    level: 2,
  },
  {
    name: 'Bronze Package',
    price: 49,
    level: 1,
  }
];

mongoose.connect('mongodb://localhost:27017/test', { useNewUrlParser: true, useUnifiedTopology: true });

const ProductSchema = new mongoose.Schema({
  name: String,
  price: Number,
  level: Number,
});

const Product = mongoose.model('Product', ProductSchema);

app.post('/products', async (req, res) => {
  const newProduct = new Product({
    name: req.body.name,
    price: req.body.price,
    level: req.body.level,
  });

  await newProduct.save();

  res.send({ message: 'Product created successfully!' });
});

app.listen(3000);
```

This app defines a simple product model with name, price, and level. You can customize the products list and their prices as needed. The app uses Mongoose to manage the database and defines routes to create new products and retrieve them.

